@startuml Sequence Diagram - Successful Payment
title Escenario 1 - Pago Exitoso (Simulator API)
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #666666
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #666666

participant "Comercio\n(Backend)" as Comercio
participant "SDK KitPagos" as SDK
participant "Simulator API\n(Fastify)" as SimAPI
participant "GatewayMockFactory" as MockFactory
participant "TransactionStore" as Store

Comercio -> SDK : createPayment(CreatePaymentRequest)
SDK -> SimAPI : POST /v1/sim/{gateway}/payments\n(Auth + Body nativo de la pasarela)
SimAPI -> MockFactory : buildApprovedResponse(gateway, request)
MockFactory -> MockFactory : Genera payload nativo\n(Wompi: {data:{id,status:"APPROVED"}},\nMercado Pago: {id,status:"approved"},\nRapyd: {data:{id,status:"CLO",paid:true}},\nKushki: {ticketNumber,details:{transactionStatus:"APPROVAL"}})
MockFactory -> Store : save(gatewayTransactionId, payload)
Store --> MockFactory : OK
MockFactory --> SimAPI : payload nativo
SimAPI --> SDK : HTTP 201 / 200 (payload nativo)
SDK -> SDK : ResponseNormalizer.normalize(payload, gateway)
SDK --> Comercio : PaymentResult(TRANSACTION: status=APPROVED)

note over Comercio, Store
  Para Wompi (punto 50): el simulador crea en PENDING
  y resuelve a APPROVED en la primera consulta de estado,
  reflejando el comportamiento asincrono de la pasarela real.
  Para Mercado Pago con PSE: devuelve REDIRECT_REQUIRED
  con redirectUrl; la consulta posterior por el id
  ORD... devuelve APPROVED.
  Para Rapyd con tarjeta: devuelve REDIRECT_REQUIRED
  al hosted checkout; simula el pago y la consulta
  devuelve APPROVED.
end note

@enduml
